  "description": "Eligibility Open to all B.Tech students across Mumbai. Students from any specialization within B.Tech are welcome. Both inter-college and inter-specialization teams are allowed. Team Formation Team size: 3–4 members . Teams must nominate a team leader for communication and coordination. Registration Fees : Group of 3: ₹400 Group of 4: ₹450 Competition Format Round 1: Problem Statement Selection & Brainstorming At 10:30 AM , problem statements (focused on community and social issues) will be distributed. A maximum of two teams can select the same problem statement , though participants are encouraged to choose unique ones. Teams will have two hours for brainstorming and preparing their solutions in a structured PPT format. Round 2: Pitching Phase Teams will present their solutions to the judges. Each team will have 7–10 minutes including Q&A to pitch their idea. Judging will be based on innovation, practicality, social impact, and presentation clarity . Event Timeline 8:30 AM – Registration of participants 9:15 AM – Inauguration ceremony 10:30 AM – Ideathon Session (Problem Statements + Brainstorming) 12:30 PM – Lunch (provided for all participants) 1:15 PM – Pitching Phase (Team Presentations) 4:00 PM – Tea Break 4:30 PM – Valedictory & Prize Distribution What’s in it for you? Winners will be awarded cash prizes and goodies . A platform to present creative, socially impactful ideas . Opportunity to collaborate with students from diverse fields. Experience that strengthens innovation, problem-solving, and presentation skills. Recognition and networking opportunities with judges, faculty, and peers.",
