    "details": "<p><strong>Eligibility</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Open to all B.Tech students across Mumbai.</li>\n<li>Students from any specialization within B.Tech are welcome.</li>\n<li>Both inter-college and inter-specialization teams are allowed.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Team Formation</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Team size: <strong>3&ndash;4 members</strong>.</li>\n<li>Teams must nominate a <strong>team leader</strong> for communication and coordination.</li>\n<li><strong>Registration Fees</strong>:\n<ul>\n<li>Group of 3: <strong>₹400</strong></li>\n<li>Group of 4: <strong>₹450</strong></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Competition Format</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Round 1: Problem Statement Selection &amp; Brainstorming</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>At <strong>10:30 AM</strong>, problem statements (focused on community and social issues) will be distributed.</li>\n<li>A maximum of <strong>two teams can select the same problem statement</strong>, though participants are encouraged to choose unique ones.</li>\n<li>Teams will have <strong>two hours</strong> for brainstorming and preparing their solutions in a structured PPT format.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Round 2: Pitching Phase</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Teams will present their solutions to the judges.</li>\n<li>Each team will have <strong>7&ndash;10 minutes including Q&amp;A</strong> to pitch their idea.</li>\n<li>Judging will be based on <strong>innovation, practicality, social impact, and presentation clarity</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Event Timeline</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>8:30 AM</strong> &ndash; Registration of participants</li>\n<li><strong>9:15 AM</strong> &ndash; Inauguration ceremony</li>\n<li><strong>10:30 AM</strong> &ndash; Ideathon Session (Problem Statements + Brainstorming)</li>\n<li><strong>12:30 PM</strong> &ndash; Lunch (provided for all participants)</li>\n<li><strong>1:15 PM</strong> &ndash; Pitching Phase (Team Presentations)</li>\n<li><strong>4:00 PM</strong> &ndash; Tea Break</li>\n<li><strong>4:30 PM</strong> &ndash; Valedictory &amp; Prize Distribution</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>What&rsquo;s in it for you?</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Winners will be awarded <strong>cash prizes and goodies</strong>.</li>\n<li>A platform to present <strong>creative, socially impactful ideas</strong>.</li>\n<li>Opportunity to collaborate with students from diverse fields.</li>\n<li>Experience that strengthens innovation, problem-solving, and presentation skills.</li>\n<li>Recognition and networking opportunities with judges, faculty, and peers.</li>\n</ul>",
